WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.725
Distance looks easy, and that’s exactly why it costs people points.

2
00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:10.150
One minute of latitude is one nautical mile, measured at the side of the chart.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.800
Use the part of the scale that’s level with your work.

4
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.600
Never use the longitude scale.

5
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.150
At New England’s latitude, how wrong would that be?

6
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.050
About a quarter too long.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.675
And that wrong answer will be sitting among the choices, waiting for you.

8
00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:30.100
Step your dividers carefully.

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.150
On a long leg, a small slip at every step adds up.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.625
And give distances to the nearest tenth of a mile.

11
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:43.525
The answer choices are often only two tenths apart, so this is not the place to round.
